# Line endings for the frontend lane.
#
# In the team repository this file sits at frontend/.gitattributes. The team
# root carries an identical `* text=auto eol=lf` rule, but main does not have
# that file yet, so on a main-based branch normalisation depends on each
# contributor's local core.autocrlf rather than on repository policy.
#
# The difference is visible: `git ls-files --eol` reports an empty attr/ column
# when nothing in the repository asks for an ending, which is how a Windows
# checkout ends up committing CRLF and turning a one-line review into a
# whole-file diff. Four machines and a Linux runner is exactly the situation
# that rule exists for.
#
# This is not a policy change. The files already sit in the index as LF; this
# makes that a guarantee rather than a property of whoever staged them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and vendored, collapsed in review so real changes stay visible.
# Matches the team root .gitattributes.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
